The hint mechanism in `config.rs` (scanning the config source and Pkl stderr on eval failure) gives targeted guidance for `check_byte_order_marker`/`fix_byte_order_marker`, `UserConfig.pkl`, `Types.Regex`, etc. — but not for `gitleaks_staged`, `knip_strict`, `pinact_v3`, or `pinact_update_v3`, the four renames this discussion announces. Those currently surface as a bare Pkl "Cannot find property" error. Adding them to the hint list (with the factory-option replacement, e.g. `(Builtins.gitleaks) { staged = true }`) would make `test/v2_migration_errors.bats` coverage match the announcement.

