`knip.strict` and `pinact.version` establish factory options nicely. It would help preset authors if common strictness toggles became factory options too (e.g. zizmor `--pedantic`, hadolint `--failure-threshold`): today the only way to get them is replacing the command under `step { … }`, which also downgrades the v2 structured `CommandSpec` (argv + effect metadata) back to an opaque shell string. A loose convention — `strict: Boolean` wherever the tool has a pedantic/strict mode — would keep those overrides declarative and preserve the effect metadata.

