{
  "updatedAt": "2026-08-28T05:41:37Z",
  "pagination": {
    "hasNextPage": false,
    "endCursor": "REDACTED"
  },
  "comments": [
    {
      "author": "risu729",
      "createdAt": "2026-08-26T12:06:23Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-08-26T12:44:05Z",
      "url": "https://github.com/jdx/hk/discussions/1261#discussioncomment-18162115",
      "body": "I maintain a shared Pkl preset ([risu729/hk-config](https://github.com/risu729/hk-config)) that wraps the builtins catalog for my repos, and migrated it against the branch schemas to see how the changes hold up in practice: [risu729/hk-config#83](https://github.com/risu729/hk-config/pull/83). Overall the direction is great — the implicit `check`/`fix`/`pre-commit` hooks matched the hook boilerplate my preset generated (including `stash = git` on pre-commit) so exactly that I could delete the helper that existed only to produce it. Findings, each checked against the branch code:\n\n### Bug: top-level `steps` rejects builtin factories\n\nIntroduced in #1255: top-level `steps` is typed `Mapping<String, Step | Group>` while `Hook.steps` and `Group.steps` in the same file use `StepDefinition`. So the headline example fails typecheck:\n\n```pkl\nsteps {\n  [\"prettier\"] = Builtins.prettier // Expected value of type `Step | Group`, but got type `Builtins#Prettier`\n}\n```\n\nReproduced by evaluating a config against `pkl/Config.pkl` from `refactor/remove-v1-interfaces` plus a `Builtins.pkl` stub in the generated factory shape. `steps: Mapping<String, StepDefinition | Group>` fixes it.\n\n### Overlook: migration hints don't cover the renamed builtin factories\n\nThe hint mechanism in `config.rs` (scanning the config source and Pkl stderr on eval failure) gives targeted guidance for `check_byte_order_marker`/`fix_byte_order_marker`, `UserConfig.pkl`, `Types.Regex`, etc. — but not for `gitleaks_staged`, `knip_strict`, `pinact_v3`, or `pinact_update_v3`, the four renames this discussion announces. Those currently surface as a bare Pkl \"Cannot find property\" error. Adding them to the hint list (with the factory-option replacement, e.g. `(Builtins.gitleaks) { staged = true }`) would make `test/v2_migration_errors.bats` coverage match the announcement.\n\n### Small builtin fix while breaking anyway: pinact glob misses root `action.yml`\n\n`pinact`'s `glob = List(\".github/workflows/*\", \"*/action.*\")`: since step globs are built without `literal_separator`, `*` crosses directories and nested metadata like `.github/actions/setup/action.yml` already matches — but a root-level `action.yml` (standalone action repos) never does, because the pattern requires a `/` before `action.`. `**/action.*` covers both.\n\n### Suggestion: a convention for strictness options\n\n`knip.strict` and `pinact.version` establish factory options nicely. It would help preset authors if common strictness toggles became factory options too (e.g. zizmor `--pedantic`, hadolint `--failure-threshold`): today the only way to get them is replacing the command under `step { … }`, which also downgrades the v2 structured `CommandSpec` (argv + effect metadata) back to an opaque shell string. A loose convention — `strict: Boolean` wherever the tool has a pedantic/strict mode — would keep those overrides declarative and preserve the effect metadata.\n\n### Docs suggestion\n\nThe factory-option + `step { … }` interaction is the main thing preset authors will reach for, e.g.:\n\n```pkl\n[\"pinact\"] = (Builtins.pinact) {\n  version = \"3\"\n  step { glob = List(\".github/workflows/*\", \"**/action.*\") }\n}\n```\n\nI verified Pkl's late binding makes the `step` amend apply on top of the version-selected step, but that's non-obvious enough to deserve an explicit example in the migration doc.\n\n*AI-assisted — Tool: Claude Code; model: anthropic/claude-fable-5; version: 2.1.241.*",
      "repliesPagination": {
        "hasNextPage": false,
        "endCursor": "Y3Vyc29yOnYyOpHOARU1Gg=="
      },
      "replies": [
        {
          "author": "risu729",
          "createdAt": "2026-08-26T19:20:17Z",
          "updatedAt": "2026-08-26T19:21:10Z",
          "url": "https://github.com/jdx/hk/discussions/1261#discussioncomment-18166882",
          "body": "I'm sorry, I didn't mean to post this. They're just nitpicks, and I don't think they will affect the design. I'll create a PR later for the pinact point, but the others don't need fixes right now.\r\n\r\nAside from them, what do you think about dropping Apple pkl CLI support? I don't think we need it, maybe for testing, but not for users."
        },
        {
          "author": "jdx",
          "createdAt": "2026-08-26T19:43:05Z",
          "updatedAt": "2026-08-26T19:43:05Z",
          "url": "https://github.com/jdx/hk/discussions/1261#discussioncomment-18167066",
          "body": "we could probably drop it"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "author": "EgoMaw",
      "createdAt": "2026-08-26T13:03:15Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-08-26T13:03:15Z",
      "url": "https://github.com/jdx/hk/discussions/1261#discussioncomment-18162746",
      "body": "I think top level steps can introduce some confusion if its not clearly conveyed what hooks they create.\r\n\r\nBuiltins having options instead of duplicating them for specific flows is a welcomed change.\r\nAnd to expand further, would that open the road for passing our own arguments over whatever the builtin currently passes, in the future?",
      "repliesPagination": {
        "hasNextPage": false,
        "endCursor": "Y3Vyc29yOnYyOpHOARUnBw=="
      },
      "replies": [
        {
          "author": "jdx",
          "createdAt": "2026-08-26T14:07:11Z",
          "updatedAt": "2026-08-26T14:07:11Z",
          "url": "https://github.com/jdx/hk/discussions/1261#discussioncomment-18163463",
          "body": "> I think top level steps can introduce some confusion if its not clearly conveyed what hooks they create.\r\n\r\nthis is mostly sugar to permit simpler configs. I'm still unsure myself since it might just be sweeping complexity under the rug.\r\n\r\n> Builtins having options instead of duplicating them for specific flows is a welcomed change.\r\n\r\nyeah, the builtin function change is the biggest change here and also probably the most necessary. We've started to add variants like `_v3` and `_staged` but the second we want more than 1 option that model is going to fall over since `_v3_staged` is going to cause obvious problems. That hasn't occurred yet but it's obvious to me it will happen.\r\n\r\n> And to expand further, would that open the road for passing our own arguments over whatever the builtin currently passes, in the future?\r\n\r\nyes but you don't need this change for that, you could write your own pkl to do that today"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "author": "bchatard",
      "createdAt": "2026-08-28T05:41:37Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-08-28T05:41:37Z",
      "url": "https://github.com/jdx/hk/discussions/1261#discussioncomment-18184182",
      "body": "I'm not sure if this is the right place to bring this up, but v2 seems like a good candidate.\r\n\r\nSince pklr is a solid replacement for the default Pkl processing when using hk, would it be possible to support the same built-ins? https://hk.jdx.dev/builtins.html#pkl",
      "repliesPagination": {
        "hasNextPage": false,
        "endCursor": null
      },
      "replies": []
    }
  ]
}

